From: leerep <leerep@163.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: add the possible_interfaces bitmap to struct phy_device

The QSDK 14.0 qca-nss-phy driver (qca8084) records the PHY interface modes
that the attached PHY switches between depending on media speed:

	qca8084_fill_possible_interfaces():
		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII, phydev->possible_interfaces);
		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX, phydev->possible_interfaces);

mainline added that field in 6.11 ("net: phy: add possible_interfaces
bitmap"), together with the phylink consumer that uses it to retrigger the
MAC configuration when the PHY switches interface mode.  The QSDK 6.6 tree
carries the field as well, so the driver builds there.

Only the field is needed to build: this kernel (6.6.88) already provides
DECLARE_PHY_INTERFACE_MASK(), PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_QUSGMII and the mask
helpers (they came in with the QUSGMII support), and the driver only writes
into the bitmap - the phylink logic that would read it is a 6.11 feature
that this kernel does not have, so the bitmap stays unused here and no
behaviour changes.  Adding the field keeps the QSDK driver source untouched
instead of patching it with a local #ifdef.

--- a/include/linux/phy.h
+++ b/include/linux/phy.h
@@ -675,6 +675,8 @@ struct phy_device {
 	u32 dev_flags;
 
 	phy_interface_t interface;
+	/* bitmap of the interface modes the PHY switches between */
+	DECLARE_PHY_INTERFACE_MASK(possible_interfaces);
 
 	/*
 	 * forced speed & duplex (no autoneg)
-- 
